  "gauge_semantics": "a gauge changes the operator to G . M.  Multiplying by m cannot shrink a frame; factoring m out can, and only when m divides every monomial of the row.  The census after gauging therefore belongs to the gauged operator, and the receipt reports each role raw frame, gauge, divisibility and residual frame rather than only a histogram",
